      "side": 1,
      "message": "Avoid src_cols truncation — use src_width * 2 directly (like ScalePlaneBox in source/scale.cc:877).\n\nBecause dx \u003d FixedDiv(src_width, dst_width) \u003d (src_width \u003c\u003c 16) / dst_width truncates toward zero, whenever (src_width \u003c\u003c 16) is not evenly divisible by dst_width, dst_width * dx is\n(src_width \u003c\u003c 16) - remainder, which makes src_cols \u003d (dst_width * dx) \u003e\u003e 16 evaluate to src_width - 1 (an odd number).\n\nFor example, with 720p chroma (src_width \u003d 640) scaled to 214x120 (By3Rounded) or 106x60 (By6):\n\n• src_width * 2 \u003d 1280 is 32-byte aligned (IS_ALIGNED(1280, 32) is true), so ScaleAddRow uses ScaleAddRow_AVX2 / ScaleAddRow_SSE2 / ScaleAddRow_NEON.\n• src_cols becomes 639, so row_samples \u003d 1278 (1278 % 16 \u003d\u003d 14), which breaks 16/32-byte SIMD alignment and forces ScaleAddRow_Any_* on every source row just to avoid accumulating 1\ntrailing UV pair (2 bytes).\n\nSince ScaleUVBox is only called when clip_x \u003d\u003d 0, we can remove src_cols and use const int row_samples \u003d src_width * 2; directly:\n\n    const int row_samples \u003d src_width * 2;\n    {\n      // Row accumulator, two uint16_t per source pixel.\n      align_buffer_64(row16, row_samples * 2);",
      "revId": "ad984ebe5f025fda439d6461ad35862d4506109a",
